{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T13:20:37Z","content":"Done. I wrote the Python code exactly as you described, compiled it, and the MP4 video is ready.\n\nClick here to watch the result:\n[MotionDemo.mp4](file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4f46c5d7-aaf4-4f5d-a8ca-eac2a671a001/scratch/media/videos/motion_demo/720p30/MotionDemo.mp4)\n\n**Here is the exact Python code I wrote to generate that video:**\n```python\nfrom manim import *\n\nclass MotionDemo(Scene):\n    def construct(self):\n        # Draw a circle\n        circle = Circle(color=BLUE)\n        self.play(Create(circle))\n        self.wait(0.5)\n        \n        # Morph it into a square\n        square = Square(color=RED)\n        self.play(Transform(circle, square))\n        self.wait(0.5)\n        \n        # Have the text 'Hello' fade in below it\n        text = Text(\"Hello\", font_size=48).next_to(square, DOWN, buff=0.5)\n        self.play(FadeIn(text))\n        \n        # Hold the final frame\n        self.wait(2)\n```\n\nAs you can see, this is 100% code-driven. I did not draw anything or generate pixels like Midjourney; I just told the computer coordinates and transition states.\n\nNow you have seen exactly how this works and what it looks like. Are we officially pivoting this conversation to YouTube video production, or are you returning to your Heat Transfer syllabus?"}
